				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Free, fast, mobile-relevant vulnerability data sources evaluated for Gt4Security. Selection criteria: **free**, **no or generous rate limits**, **daily or near-realtime updates**, **simple REST/JSON**, and **mobile coverage** (iOS, Android platform, mobile app libraries).\n\nSources evaluated:\n\n1. **NVD API v2** — `services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0`\n2. **OSV.dev** — `api.osv.dev`\n3. **GitHub Advisory Database** — `api.github.com/advisories`\n4. **CIRCL Vulnerability Lookup** — `vulnerability.circl.lu`\n5. **Vulners** — `vulners.com`\n6. **Android Security Bulletins** — `source.android.com/docs/security/bulletin`\n7. **OSSF Malicious Packages** — `github.com/ossf/malicious-packages` (mirrored into OSV.dev)\n\nSee the comparison table below."
			},
			{
