				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Recommendation\n\n**Primary CVE sources (integrate first):**\n\n1. **OSV.dev** — Single unauthenticated JSON API with a dedicated `Android` ecosystem (ingested directly from Android Security Bulletins) plus Swift, Maven, and Pub. Zero documented rate limits. Lowest friction for a ZnClient-based tool.\n2. **NVD API v2** — Authoritative CPE-based coverage for iOS / iPadOS and device vendor firmware that OSV's ecosystem model doesn't cleanly express. Free API key gives 50 req / 30s — more than enough for incremental `lastModStartDate` polling.\n\n**Complementary source:**\n\n- **OSSF Malicious Packages (via OSV.dev mirror)** — already reachable through the same `api.osv.dev` client, so it adds malicious-package signal for bundled JS / Python dependencies in mobile apps at **zero integration cost**.\n\n**Skipped and why:**\n\n- **Vulners** — API-key friction, credit-metered free tier\n- **GitHub Advisory DB** — weak mobile platform fit, duplicates OSV for Swift / Pub\n- **CIRCL** — duplicates NVD\n- **Android Bulletins (direct scraping)** — OSV already ingests them in structured form"
			}
		]
	},
